addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A sanitary ware characterized as comprising an earthenware substrate, a first colored cover coat enamel layer formed on the surface thereof, a second transparent cover coat enamel layer formed on the first enamel layer, and an engobe layer formed between the surface of the earthenware substrate and the first enamel layer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une installation sanitaire comprenant un substrat en terre cuite, une première couche colorée de revêtement émaillé à la surface du substrat, une seconde couche transparente de revêtement émaillé à la surface de la première couche émaillée, et une couche d'engobe entre la surface du substrat et la première couche émaillée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>